{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790453217,"nonce":"naigl5VgpDC2bPnVVpza3XBbVVI=","message":"ae07899 replaces the approach of 7f422e4 (separate plugin instances with their own memory, string bridges, a dispatch import) with Ash's model from ash docs/wasm/hdlls.md:\n\n- A native library is a dylink.0 side module sharing the program's memory and table. The plugin ABI is unchanged: a foreign method is extern \"C\" fn(*mut VM) against wlift_abi, as on native.\n- wlift --aot --aot-target wasm32-* places each library beside the output as \u003clib\u003e.wasm: a side module from the package is copied; a PIC .a (RUSTFLAGS=-C relocation-model=pic -C target-feature=+mutable-globals, -Z build-std=std,panic_abort) is linked into one with rust-lld --experimental-pic -shared --unresolved-symbols=import-dynamic --whole-archive, exporting the #!symbol names the program uses (WLIFT_WASM_LD overrides the linker).\n- link_wasm reads the side modules beside its output and links with hdll_imports/hdll_data plus malloc, as ash --build does.\n- Runtime: foreign_wasm's loader falls back to ash_host_dlopen/ash_host_dlsym; a symbol is a table index used as the ForeignCFn. The imports sit behind forwards only a program with foreign classes installs (wlift_aot_set_native_loader), so the runtime links alone and plain programs import only WASI.\n- tests/wasm_aot.rs's host is a port of ash_wasm_runtime's native/dylink.rs loader, with a WAT side module covering a numeric call, the library's own data at __memory_base, and a string pointer shared with the program.\n- Checked by hand: plugins/wlift_noise as a PIC .a, through the CLI into a side module, run under that host; same values as the native dylib.\n\nLeft:\n- hatch's workflow: build each plugin's PIC .a for wasm32-wasip1 and link its side module, and declare it under native_libs.\n- The existing browser plugins (wlift_window_web, wlift_gpu_web, wlift_hello) use the separate-instance bridge ABI and need porting to side modules.\n- Running needs an Ash host (ash-wasm-run, caribou's, or the browser loader Ash lists as not done); WrenLift's programs are WASI commands with _start.","files":null}]}